<!--
  Fixture provenance (guardrail 3: real-but-public government data).
  Source: U.S. Geological Survey (USGS) FDSNWS event service, KML format.
  URL: https://earthquake.usgs.gov/fdsnws/event/1/query?format=kml&starttime=2024-01-01&endtime=2024-01-02&minmagnitude=5
  Fetched: 2026-07-07. Query window is a fixed historical range so the
  result set is stable. Trimming step: kept the first 3 <Placemark> elements
  from the returned <Document>; nothing else altered. Placemarks carry <name>,
  <description> (CDATA), and a <Point> whose 3rd coordinate (altitude) the
  import.kml reader drops to 2D lon/lat.
-->
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
<Document>
  <name>USGS Earthquakes</name>
  <Style id="circle"><IconStyle><scale>0.6</scale></IconStyle></Style>
